  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1226 AM EST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nA trough over Ontario will cut off a closed low over the Great Lakes \novernight and Friday morning, pushing a cold front toward our area \nthat will move through late in the day. Moisture will be very \nlimited and shallow, but a few light showers or sprinkles are \npossible in the evening, as depicted by the HRRR and RRFS. Will add \nsome low PoPs to the northern Plateau and VA counties bordering KY. \n\nWith high pressure centered over the central Plains and a northerly \nflow from the Great Lakes directed into the Appalachians, \ntemperatures will drop behind the front on Saturday. Highs will be \nmainly in the upper 50s to lower 60s, with lows on Saturday night in \nthe 30s. We will see dry conditions and a gradual warm up for early \nnext week, with plenty of sunshine and highs mostly in the 60s \nthrough Wednesday. Looking toward the end of next week, there is a \nchance of a deep upper trough bringing much colder temperatures to \nthe region.",
